|---|---|---|---|---|
| F1 | P1 | IP/cpu_m1/rtl/pipeline_v2/ch2_lab08e/cpu_m1_top.v:113 | Waited D access can be re-issued after ready. | If `d_fire` sees `dbus_ready=0`, `d_busy` holds req; on the ready edge `d_busy` clears while `core` still holds EX/MEM under `mem_stall` (`core.v:711`). Next cycle `mem_stall=0`, same `d_mem_valid` is still visible, so `d_fire` asserts again. Stores duplicate on the bus; normal RAM may hide it, MMIO will not. |
| F2 | P1 | IP/cpu_m1/rtl/pipeline_v2/ch2_lab08e/csr.v:145 | `mcycle` mutates during `mem_stall`. | ADR-0005 requires every architectural side-effect suppressed during freeze. `wb_instr_retired`/CSR writes/traps are gated in `core.v`, but `cycle_cnt <= cycle_cnt + 1` is unconditional, so CSR-visible state diverges under waits. |
| F3 | P2 | IP/cpu_m1/rtl/pipeline_v2/ch2_lab08e/cpu_m1_top.v:90 | Boot-prime is not reset-clean. | `ibus_req` depends on uninitialized `primed` before first reset clock, and `primed <= 1` at line 109 can override the reset assignment because it is outside the reset `else`; boot fetch behavior depends on `ibus_ready` during reset. |

## not-covered
- `tb_equiv.v` checks only commit-index `{pc, rd, wdata}`; it does not count I/D bus transactions, so duplicate stores pass.
- It does not validate CSR-visible `mcycle/minstret/mepc/mcause/mtval` under waits.
- It does not run the misalign program or assert mcause 4/6 and no misaligned bus request.
- It does not prove cycle/bit-identical 0-wait behavior, only commit-stream equivalence.
- Firmware does include loads/stores/branches/div/RVC, but only 81 commits and RAM-only stores; no MMIO/non-idempotent store coverage.
- Bare-core==Spike is not proven by `tb_equiv.v`; that claim depends on the separate re-validation.

